From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:54:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 80/93] dt-bindings: display: apple,dcp: add
 apple,merged-mode-limit

The platform's limit on merged modes belongs to the external display
coprocessors of a machine, not to its sleep. Give it a property of
their nodes.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>

[re-cut onto the K114s r3d tree]
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
index b06974140da..e58fbe5fa3e 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,dcp.yaml
@@ -102,6 +102,13 @@ properties:
       The driver takes it as the "secure" mailbox. Elsewhere the port is the
       second entry of mboxes.
 
+  apple,merged-mode-limit:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      The platform's limit on merged modes applies to this external display
+      coprocessor. A display takes a second coprocessor as its pair only
+      while one is left for every external display that is present.
+
   iommus:
     maxItems: 1
 
